Backport of upstream DXVK 1676dcaf342a9b13af86c0464ad46235687727a6
("[dxvk] Fix build failure with Clang 22", closes doitsujin/dxvk#5545).

    Pass the default-constructed key explicitly instead of using an empty
    std::tuple() with std::piecewise_construct, which Clang/LLVM 22 rejects
    due to stricter parameter pack validation.

The same libc++ change ships in Apple clang 21 / Xcode 27, so DXVK fails to
build on current macOS without this. libc++'s new __try_key_extraction fast
path for unordered_map::emplace forms `tuple_element<0, _Tuple1>::type` while
substituting its own enable_if; for _Tuple1 = std::tuple<> that instantiates
tuple_element<0, tuple<>>, which hard-errors inside the instantiation rather
than in the immediate context, so the `tuple_size<_Tuple1>::value == 1` guard
beside it never discards the overload.

fbraz3/dxvk has not picked the upstream commit up (its master still carries
std::tuple()), and this repo pins an older fork commit still. The changed
line here is byte-identical to upstream's, so once the fork rebases, the
reverse-check in cmake/apply-dxvk-patch.cmake passes and this patch
self-disables instead of conflicting.

diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_pipemanager.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_pipemanager.cpp
index 84a07c1f..47df13b2 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_pipemanager.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_pipemanager.cpp
@@ -443,7 +443,7 @@ namespace dxvk {
 
     auto iter = m_shaderLibraries.emplace(
       std::piecewise_construct,
-      std::tuple(),
+      std::tuple(key),
       std::tuple(m_device, this, key, layout));
     return &iter.first->second;
   }
